  "_comment": "Devin hook payloads shaped against Devin CLI 3000.6.7 (260a97c8). RE-MEASURED 2026-09-02 by installing a stdin-capture hook in a trusted workspace and running a live non-interactive session, which corrected three things the earlier corpus got wrong: every tool payload carries tool_use_id (previously absent here), NO payload carries cwd (previously present on all of them), and NO payload carries transcript_path — which is why aidlc-fold-usage.ts is not wired on this harness: it exits at its `if (!transcriptPath)` guard on every invocation. Devin's stdin envelope is otherwise Claude Code's — hook_event_name, tool_name, tool_input, tool_response, session_id — which is why the adapter is a name translator and not a payload reshaper (contrast Codex, which reshapes a genuinely foreign envelope). Two Devin-specific facts the corpus encodes: tool names are lowercase snake_case (exec, edit, apply_patch, run_subagent, todo_write), and ask_user_question is NOT a documented matchable tool name, so the picker arrives only on the matcher-free PreToolUse arm and is never named in a hooks.v1.json matcher. Volatile values (ids) are anonymized; every KEY is as delivered.",
